      "summaries": {
        "en": "BioBERT-base-cased-v1.1 is a specialized BERT model pre-trained on biomedical literature to understand complex medical terminology and relationships. Its key innovation is domain-specific pre-training on PubMed abstracts and PMC articles, enabling it to capture biomedical context better than general language models. Researchers can fine-tune it for tasks like named entity recognition, relation extraction, or question answering on clinical texts using Hugging Face's transformers library. This makes it particularly valuable for biomedical NLP applications where accurate interpretation of technical terms is crucial.",
        "zh": "BioBERT-base-cased-v1.1 是一个专门针对生物医学领域预训练的BERT模型，旨在理解复杂的医学术语和概念关系。其核心创新在于使用PubMed摘要和PMC全文进行领域特定预训练，相比通用语言模型能更好地捕捉生物医学上下文语义。研究人员可通过Hugging Face的transformers库对其进行微调，应用于临床文本的命名实体识别、关系抽取或问答系统等任务。该模型特别适合需要精确解析医学术语的生物医学自然语言处理应用，为医疗文本分析提供了专业化的语言理解能力。",
        "es": "BioBERT-base-cased-v1.1 is a specialized BERT model pre-trained on biomedical literature to understand complex medical terminology and relationships. Its key innovation is domain-specific pre-training on PubMed abstracts and PMC articles, enabling it to capture biomedical context better than general language models. Researchers can fine-tune it for tasks like named entity recognition, relation extraction, or question answering on clinical texts using Hugging Face's transformers library. This makes it particularly valuable for biomedical NLP applications where accurate interpretation of technical terms is crucial.",
        "sections": {
          "why": "biobert-base-cased-v1.1 stands out for transformers, pytorch, and endpoints_compatible in real-world workflows.",
          "what": "BioBERT-base-cased-v1.1 is a specialized BERT model pre-trained on biomedical literature to understand complex medical terminology and relationships. Its key innovation is domain-specific pre-training on PubMed abstracts and PMC articles, enabling it to capture biomedical context better than general language models. Researchers can fine-tune it for tasks like named entity recognition, relation extraction, or question answering on clinical texts using Hugging Face's transformers library. This makes it particularly valuable for biomedical NLP applications where accurate interpretation of technical terms is crucial.",
          "how": "Review https://huggingface.co/dmis-lab/biobert-base-cased-v1.1 for docs, run starter examples, and integrate with your pipeline or evaluation stack."
        }
